      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Per-source offsets only have an effect on parent constraints, and are ignored by the other constraint types where a single offset is defined for the entire constraint instead. This matches how Unity constraints work.\n\nThe per-source offsets were accidentally exposed in the inspector for all contraint types in 3.6.2-constraints.3 and have now correctly been hidden for all types except parent constraints as of 3.6.2-constraints.4. Apologies for any confusion this might have caused!\n\nFor the scenario you've described, you could try animating the value of the rotation offset on your rotation constraint instead.",
