  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The constraint documentation for Rotation Constraints describes the \"offset at rest\" and \"rotation offset\" very briefly (though the explanation for \"rotation offset\" is not very clear).\n\nHowever, the offsets available under the \"source\" are not documented at all, and not shown in the sample image included in the docs.  What do these do?  When do they apply?  Do they add to or overwrite the base offsets?\n\nDo they even work?  I haven't been able to get them to do anything, but without docs, I'm not entirely sure what they should be doing.\n\nI have a specific case where in most cases I need source #1 to apply, but via toggle I want source #2 to apply but the source transform is rotated 90 degrees from the source in #1, and I need to take this into account, but it's not clear how to do this, if it's even possible.",
